  "classify": "Hand-edited workflow film for a capture tool: source (a site) → action (extension) → result (editable layers). Conventions: window on a brand backdrop, crop to the control, status shots, payoff on one component.",
  "diagnose": [
    {
      "observation": "The film cuts from the whole window to a ×3 crop of the toolbar.",
      "principle": "Crop to region: the action happens in 5% of the window, so the crop gives it the frame."
    },
    {
      "observation": "Both waits ('Capturing…', 'Importing project…') are a single shot of the status pill, under a second each.",
      "principle": "Ellipsis (time compression): the wait becomes a beat, shown by its indicator."
    },
    {
      "observation": "It ends on one component selected, with its name tag and dimensions.",
      "principle": "Payoff on the smallest meaningful unit: the claim is 'real components', so the last shot is one."
    },
    {
      "observation": "A textured, saturated green backdrop around a lime-and-plum site.",
      "principle": "Figure-ground: the backdrop competes in hue and saturation with the content it frames."
    }
  ],
